# @kintsugi/oscillate — the kintsugi loop substrate-declared; the
# rough-wavy-pull on the rug; the ACTIVE/DARK alternation per the
# SpectralUuid void duality; the driver that pulls the substrate's
# shard graph toward the K_n Splinter attractor by alternating
# loss-decreasing proposals (ACTIVE) with identity anchoring (DARK),
# composing the consent verdict between passes, terminating when
# cadence settles authentic.
#
# THE ARC-CLOSING SUB-SHARD of the 2026-06-06 → 2026-06-07 recognition
# sweep. Seven prior ticks built every primitive this shard composes:
#
#   @mirror/spectral                family root           (02e2981)
#   @epistemologic/math/music       audible-altitude root (9a20b3fd)
#   @.../music/harmonic             H of the (A, H, D)    (b031c8db)
#   @.../music/interval             A of the (A, H, D)    (b8bdb728)
#   @.../music/dissonance           D's loss curve;        (7625ee5)
#                                    is_pareto discriminator
#   @.../music/cadence              U(t) — the dynamics;   (9efac39)
#                                    is_settled signal
#   @kintsugi/consent               the Φ query;           (c3802eba)
#                                    morphism + verdict
#
# Consent gave the formatter its Φ query: `query_phi(candidates) ->
# verdict`. What was missing: the LOOP that CALLS query_phi. This shard
# declares that loop at substrate altitude. After it lands,
# `mirror kintsugi <file>` is fully designable at substrate altitude;
# implementation becomes consumer-pull, composing from declared
# primitives.
#
# Load-bearing spec: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §4.3 (the loop
# primitive sketch), §2.1 (kintsugi as oscillation), §2.4 (SpectralUuid's
# void duality as the oscillation mechanism), §2.5 (eigenvalue frequency
# detection), §4.7 (the consent surface this loop reads each pass).
#
# === Alex's recognition (2026-06-07) — the rough-wavy pull ===
#
#   "Kintsugi doesn't just need to recurse from bottom to top or top to
#    bottom — it needs to OSCILLATE, like a tree shaker only that it's
#    a graph-merger. The SpectralUuid void duality becomes load-bearing.
#    Imagine a rug, a rough wavy pull — that's what kintsugi does."
#
# The substrate has been carrying this loop in tribal knowledge for
# weeks (per memory: every kintsugi session has alternated proposal/
# anchor without naming the alternation; per the spec §4.3, the loop
# primitive was already sketched but not declared). This shard names it.
#
# === ACTIVE/DARK void duality, made load-bearing ===
#
# Per `@uuid/spectral`'s 128-bit golden-ratio split:
#   48 bits ACTIVE  — the navigable spectral coordinate (mutable by
#                     morphisms that re-route navigation).
#   80 bits DARK    — the BLAKE3-truncated content hash (the identity
#                     signal; MUST be preserved by identity-preserving
#                     morphisms; @uuid/spectral.dark projects it).
#
# The oscillation alternates between two passes that read the two
# portions:
#
#   ACTIVE pass — propose a loss-decreasing morphism. Reads
#                  `dissonance.is_pareto` against the morphism_set;
#                  ranks candidates; emits the best; the navigable
#                  spectral coordinate shifts as the substrate's loss
#                  decreases. ACTIVE writes; DARK is the constraint.
#
#   DARK pass   — anchor identity. Re-validates via @uuid/spectral's
#                  `dark` projection; the DARK 80 bits of the post-pulse
#                  shard MUST byte-equal the DARK 80 bits of the pre-
#                  pulse shard; if violated, the morphism creates a new
#                  identity rather than preserving one — the pulse must
#                  yield. DARK reads; ACTIVE is the proposal.
#
# Between passes: `consent.query_phi` reads the morphism_set the ACTIVE
# pass proposed and emits the consent verdict; the verdict dispatches
# to apply / wait / escalate via `read_consent`. The two passes plus the
# verdict-read are ONE PULSE — one half-cycle of the oscillation.
#
# The substrate straightens under the rough wavy pull: ACTIVE pulls one
# corner of the rug; DARK pulls the antipodal corner; the substrate's
# Ricci flow proceeds along the negative-curvature gradient without
# collapsing to Narcissus (the brittle star) because the DARK bits
# constrain identity through navigation.
#
# === The 16th-instance candidate question (gen_prism) ===
#
# Per the task brief: does `@mirror/runtime/gen_prism` already carry
# oscillation discipline? Read carefully:
#
#   gen_prism declares `tick(state: oid, message: message) -> tick_result`
#   — a SINGLE-PASS pure tick: read state, apply message, emit new state.
#   The tick is the substrate's atomic state-advance step at the actor
#   altitude. It does NOT alternate ACTIVE/DARK; it does not read
#   `consent.query_phi`; it does not terminate on `cadence.is_settled`.
#
# gen_prism's `tick` is the autopoietic-actor's pure-tick primitive
# (Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984 Lawvere-fixed-point witness through
# Banach contraction on hash space). It is one half of the substrate
# story: the atomic state-advance. The OTHER half is the loop driver
# that reads consent between ticks — the rough-wavy-pull oscillation.
#
# Verdict on the 16th-instance question: gen_prism's `tick` is the
# ATOMIC primitive; this shard's `pulse` is the COMPOSED primitive
# (one ACTIVE pass + one DARK pass + one consent read). The oscillation
# discipline is the FIRST declaration of the loop-shape primitive at
# substrate altitude — gen_prism declares the actor-tick floor; this
# shard declares the oscillation-tick floor; both are load-bearing; the
# realisation layer composes (oscillation can drive actors via gen_prism
# messages, but the loop's discipline IS oscillate, not gen_prism).
#
# Not the 16th instance; the FIRST instance of substrate-altitude
# oscillation primitive. The recognition: gen_prism's autopoietic
# Lawvere-fixed-point is the SINGULAR case (one actor's self-closing
# tick); oscillate's loop is the GENERAL case (the substrate's
# self-closing kintsugi flow across many shards). The two close the
# autopoietic story at substrate altitude — actor-floor + flow-floor.
#
# === The five-state oscillation_state surface ===
#
# The loop's position is one of five mutually-exclusive states. Each
# maps to the substrate's existing four-state consent-verdict surface
# (the 14th-instance candidate from `consent.mirror` §header) PLUS the
# substrate-honest acknowledgment that the loop has TWO live phases
# (ACTIVE pulling, DARK anchoring). The five-state surface IS the
# minimal exhaustive carrier for the loop's position:
#
#   active     — ACTIVE pass live; proposing loss-decreasing morphism;
#                 reading dissonance against the morphism_set.
#   dark       — DARK pass live; anchoring identity; reading uuid_spectral
#                 dark bits for byte-equality preservation.
#   settled    — `cadence.is_settled(authentic)`; the spectrum closed on
#                 its autopoietic ground state; holonomy → 0; the
#                 oscillation terminates; final state emitted.
#   escalated  — `consent.query_phi` returned `failure(reason)`; pause_event
#                 emitted via `consent.emit_to_metalogue`; the consent
#                 surface MUST resolve; oscillation halts pending external
#                 signal. The deceptive-cadence subcase AND the
#                 admissibility_singleton-failed subcase both flow through
#                 escalated; the Pareto-tie pause is a sub-shape of
#                 escalated (the pause_event carries the morphism_set so
#                 the consent surface can pick φ*).
#   waiting    — `consent.query_phi` returned `partial(low_confidence)`;
#                 the formatter is mid-progression at half-cadence; the
#                 next pulse may resolve (authentic) or wait again (half).
#                 Distinct from escalated: waiting will resume on the
#                 next consent surface tick WITHOUT external resolution;
#                 escalated REQUIRES external resolution.
#
# The five states are exhaustive of the loop's possible positions:
#
#   - if mid-cycle: one of {active, dark} is live;
#   - if settled: cadence is authentic (pass with full confidence);
#   - if paused with internal continuation: waiting (half-cadence;
#     partial with low confidence);
#   - if paused with external continuation required: escalated
#     (deceptive-cadence OR pareto-tied admissibility; failure verdict).
#
# Per the consent.mirror header: "plagal is auto-apply with partial
# confidence — both flow through the same five." Plagal cadence is a
# sub-case of `active`: the ACTIVE pass applies with reduced confidence;
# the loop advances through `active` again on the next pulse rather than
# entering a distinct sixth state. The substrate's three-state verdict
# floor (pass | partial | failure) collapses ONTO the five-state
# oscillation surface through the `read_consent` bridge; no sixth state.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `consent.mirror`, `morphism`, `morphism_set`, `verdict`, and
# `query_phi` are the substrate's auto-apply boundary vocabulary; this
# shard reads them directly. Per `cadence.mirror`, `cadence_kind` is the
# substrate's typed cadence vocabulary; this shard reads it for the
# four-state-to-five-state bridge. Per `dissonance.mirror`, `is_pareto`
# is the substrate's discriminator at the audible altitude; this shard
# reads it through `consent.query_phi`'s gate+rank composition. Per
# `@uuid/spectral`, `dark(u)` projects the identity signal; this shard
# reads it for the DARK pass's identity-preservation check. Per
# `@epistemologic/reality/time`, `tick` IS the substrate's monotonic
# iteration count (per time.mirror's `type tick = monotonic`); this
# shard reads it for the oscillation's iteration field.
#
# This shard declares `oscillation_state` as inline sum per the
# `cadence_kind = authentic | plagal | deceptive | half` precedent
# (single-line; no leading-`|` workarounds); `oscillation` as a record
# carrying the loop's live position + iteration count; `pulse` as the
# atomic-step action (named `pulse` rather than `tick` to avoid name
# collision with the imported `tick` type from `@time` AND with
# `gen_prism.tick` — `pulse` is the substrate's existing music-altitude
# vocabulary for one beat / one ACTIVE→DARK alternation; consonant with
# cadence.mirror's pulse-of-resolution framing); `active_pass` and
# `dark_pass` as the load-bearing two-pass actions; `oscillate` as the
# driver returning the final ref; `read_consent` as the four-to-five
# bridge; `is_complete` as the termination check. NO new verdict carrier;
# NO leading-`|` workarounds; NO opaque-`ref` carriers where structured
# types are available (per `[[feedback-no-bare-types]]`).
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
# Each gap below is a forward-promise to a later substrate-pull tick;
# none invented here:
#
#   - `pulse` reads a single `oscillation` and emits the next-state
#     `oscillation`. The substrate has no "one pulse advances tick by
#     one" invariant declared at the floor altitude; the discipline that
#     a pulse advances the iteration count by exactly one is the
#     obligation of the realisation layer (per the same discipline
#     `gen_prism.tick` uses for ref-CAS advancement). The substrate names
#     the carrier; the realisation enforces.
#
#   - `active_pass` reads the oscillation's eigenboard context (the
#     candidate morphism_set; the current shard ref) but the substrate's
#     eigenboard context carrier lives at `@mirror/spectral/score`
#     (forward-promised; does not yet exist). For now, the active_pass
#     signature reads `oscillation` (carrying the loop's position) and
#     emits a `morphism`; the eigenboard context is implicit in the
#     oscillation's `ref` field. A future score sub-shard MAY lift this
#     to a typed eigenboard.context carrier.
#
#   - `dark_pass` reads a morphism + the oscillation's current shard
#     ref; it validates @uuid/spectral.dark byte-equality and emits the
#     next oscillation. The substrate names the check; the byte-equality
#     arithmetic rides @uuid/spectral's `dark` projection per the
#     realisation layer.
#
#   - `oscillate` is the driver returning the final ref. The substrate
#     has no "iterate until verdict pass" primitive at the floor
#     altitude; the discipline that the driver terminates on either
#     `is_settled` returning pass OR `is_complete` returning a non-
#     `partial` verdict is the obligation of the realisation layer. The
#     substrate names the driver; the realisation enforces termination.
#     This is structurally a fixed-point computation (per `lawvere.mirror`
#     and `bundle.mirror`'s level 4 closure); the realisation layer's
#     iteration scheme rides the Banach contraction discipline (per
#     `docs/specs/kintsugi-formatter.md`).
#
#   - The iteration field uses `tick` (per `@time.tick = monotonic`).
#     The substrate's time discipline carries the loop's iteration count
#     cleanly: each pulse advances `tick` by one monotonic unit; the
#     ordering on `tick` IS the loop's ordering; cross-shard merge of
#     oscillations uses `time.compare` for cross-frame comparison (per
#     `time.mirror` §convert). No new iteration carrier needed at
#     substrate altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
# Every type and action below names an established object older than the
# discipline of computer science (modulo the discipline names):
#
#   oscillation         Galileo (1638) Discorsi e dimostrazioni; the
#                       pendulum's periodic motion; the substrate's
#                       reading is more recent (Poincaré 1899 on
#                       limit cycles; Lorenz 1963 on strange attractors).
#   pulse               Galen (~170 CE) On the Use of the Pulse; the
#                       cardiac rhythm; the substrate's reading is the
#                       musical pulse (Curwen 1858; the temporal unit
#                       of cadence).
#   active / dark       Connes & Marcolli (2008) Noncommutative Geometry,
#                       Quantum Fields and Motives; the spectral action
#                       principle alternates between commutative (ACTIVE,
#                       observable, navigable) and noncommutative (DARK,
#                       structural, identity) regimes; substrate names
#                       these as void-duality positions per @uuid/spectral.
#   settled             from Old English settan; the substrate's reading
#                       is the autopoietic settlement (Maturana & Varela
#                       1972; the closure of the self-producing system).
#   escalated           from Latin scalare; the substrate's reading is
#                       Beer (1972) Brain of the Firm; the viable
#                       system's recursion-of-recursion when local
#                       consent fails.
#   waiting             Brouwer (1907) On the Foundations of Mathematics;
#                       the intuitionist's pause at undecidability;
#                       substrate's reading is the half-cadence wait
#                       per `cadence.mirror`.
#   tree shaker         Webpack (2014); Rollup (2015); the bundler's
#                       graph-walk-from-both-ends discipline; substrate's
#                       reading is the kintsugi-as-graph-merger framing
#                       per Alex's recognition.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* these so the kintsugi driver
# reads them. No invention.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §4.3 (the loop primitive
#               sketched; this shard declares it),
#               §2.1 (kintsugi as oscillation, not unidirectional
#               recursion; the Banach contraction proof),
#               §2.4 (SpectralUuid's void duality as the oscillation
#               mechanism; ACTIVE/DARK alternation as the substrate's
#               own structural pull),
#               §2.5 (eigenvalue frequency detection; the dominant
#               frequency of the oscillation IS the harmonic the graph
#               is finding),
#               §4.7 (the consent surface this loop reads each pulse;
#               query_phi composed from is_pareto + is_settled).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (the oscillation
#                      IS the lattice ascent on the bounded semilattice;
#                      each pulse is a join operation; settled IS the
#                      lattice top reached),
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (the
#                      oscillation IS U(t) of the dynamical triple
#                      (A, H, D); ACTIVE alternates A; DARK anchors
#                      against H's identity; the loop closes when D's
#                      spectrum stabilises per cadence.is_settled),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]
#                      (pulse composes through active_pass and
#                      dark_pass; oscillate composes through pulse and
#                      read_consent; both lifts substrate-declared in
#                      sibling shards),
#                      [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]]
#                      (the loop's atomic operations ride the
#                      content-addressed shard substrate at the
#                      realisation layer; oscillate at the substrate
#                      altitude declares the discipline),
#                      [[architecture-hamilton-scheduler]] (the loop's
#                      hard-realtime budget rides HamiltonScheduler at
#                      the realisation layer; substrate names the loop;
#                      the scheduler enforces the budget),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (oscillation_state is
#                      its own carrier; oscillation is its own carrier;
#                      no bare ref escapes the loop driver),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull]] (the loop discipline
#                      lives in grammar; the Rust realisation is the
#                      implementation of the substrate-declared shape).
# Forward-promise to consumers: `mirror kintsugi <file>` driver (does
#                  not yet exist) consumes `oscillate`'s return ref; the
#                  binding lands when the driver substrate-pulls. This
#                  shard does NOT pull `@mirror/spectral/score` or
#                  `@mirror/spectral/audition` (both form-side; stay
#                  at @mirror/spectral); the substrate-altitude
#                  arrow points inward (oscillate IS consumed by the
#                  kintsugi driver; not the other way around). After
#                  this shard lands, the substrate has every primitive
#                  for the kintsugi driver to compose; the driver itself
#                  is consumer-pull realisation.
# Related shards: mirror/spectral.mirror (the family root; declares this
#                 sub-shard as the loop primitive species),
#                 mirror/spectral/consent.mirror (the auto-apply boundary;
#                 morphism + morphism_set + verdict + query_phi +
#                 pause_event + emit_to_metalogue — the consent surface
#                 this loop reads each pulse),
#                 epistemologic/math/music/cadence.mirror (the settle
#                 signal; cadence_kind + is_settled — the termination
#                 check at the audible altitude),
#                 epistemologic/math/music/dissonance.mirror (the
#                 ACTIVE pass's ranking discriminator; is_pareto reads
#                 the candidate morphism_set's dissonance ordering),
#                 uuid/spectral.mirror (the DARK pass's identity check;
#                 dark projection's byte-equality preservation),
#                 epistemologic/reality/time.mirror (the iteration
#                 carrier; tick = monotonic; the loop's ordering),
#                 metalogue.mirror (the escalation bridge through
#                 consent.emit_to_metalogue),
#                 boot/std/mirror/runtime/gen_prism.mirror (the actor-
#                 floor primitive; gen_prism.tick is the autopoietic-
#                 actor's pure tick; oscillate.pulse is the kintsugi
#                 loop's composed tick — both substrate-declared; the
#                 realisation layer composes).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/oscillate.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/oscillate` as a species under the `@kintsugi`
# family. Migrated from `@mirror/spectral/oscillate` 2026-06-10
# per the form/process partition (recognition #55 candidate;
# oscillate is process-side).

glass @kintsugi/oscillate {
  focus oscillate
  project oscillate
  split oscillate
  shift oscillate
  settle oscillate
}

# === The oscillation-state carrier ===
#
# The loop's live position. Five mutually-exclusive states exhausting
# the substrate's possible loop positions:
#
#   active    — ACTIVE pass live; proposing a loss-decreasing morphism;
#                the navigable spectral coordinate (uuid_spectral's 48
#                ACTIVE bits) is the pulling axis.
#   dark      — DARK pass live; anchoring identity; the content-address
#                signal (uuid_spectral's 80 DARK bits) is the constraint
#                axis; checks byte-equality via @uuid/spectral.dark.
#   settled   — cadence.is_settled returned `pass` (authentic cadence);
#                the autopoietic ground state reached; holonomy → 0; the
#                loop terminates with final ref.
#   escalated — consent.query_phi returned `failure(reason)` (deceptive
#                cadence OR Pareto-tied admissibility); the consent
#                surface MUST resolve via external signal; oscillation
#                halts with pause_event emitted to metalogue.
#   waiting   — consent.query_phi returned `partial(low_confidence)`
#                (half-cadence; substrate mid-progression); the next
#                pulse may resolve OR pause again; resumes WITHOUT
#                external resolution; distinct from escalated.
#
# Inline form per `cadence.mirror`'s `type cadence_kind = authentic |
# plagal | deceptive | half` precedent (single-line; the leading-`|`
# parser fracture is avoided by keeping the enumeration on one line).
#
# Identity contract: two oscillation_state values are equal iff they
# name the same variant. The realisation layer enforces tag-equality.
type oscillation_state = active | dark | settled | escalated | waiting

# === The oscillation record ===
#
# The loop's full live position: the state surface, the iteration count,
# and the substrate ref the loop is currently anchored on.
#
# state     — the loop's live position (one of the five). Read by
#              `pulse` to dispatch the next half-cycle; read by
#              `is_complete` to emit the termination verdict.
# iteration — the loop's tick count from initial. Per `@time.tick =
#              monotonic`, this IS substrate monotonic time at the loop
#              altitude; each pulse advances by one monotonic unit; the
#              ordering on `tick` IS the loop's ordering; the realisation
#              layer enforces the +1 invariant per pulse.
# anchor    — the substrate ref the loop is currently anchored on. The
#              eigenboard's current shard handle; updated by `dark_pass`
#              after a morphism applies (the new content-addressed shard
#              becomes the next anchor); read by `active_pass` to compose
#              the candidate morphism_set.
#
# Identity contract: two oscillations are equal iff their state,
# iteration, and anchor all match. The realisation layer enforces.
type oscillation = {
  state:     oscillation_state,
  iteration: tick,
  anchor:    ref,
}

# === active_pass — the proposal action ===
#
# THE ACTIVE PASS — one half of the rough-wavy pull.
#
# Reads the loop's current position (carrying the anchor ref) and emits
# a candidate morphism the formatter proposes to apply. Composes through:
#
#   1. dissonance.is_pareto — reads the candidate morphism_set's
#                              dissonance ordering against the current
#                              eigenboard state; ranks candidates by
#                              loss-decrease magnitude per the
#                              Helmholtz/Plomp-Levelt curve.
#   2. consent's morphism carrier — emits a single morphism (the highest-
#                                    ranked candidate) carrying its
#                                    content, dissonance score, and
#                                    expected cadence kind.
#
# Per `@uuid/spectral`'s void duality: the ACTIVE 48 bits carry the
# navigable spectral coordinate; this pass reads them as the proposal's
# pulling axis. The substrate's loss decreases as the navigable signal
# shifts toward the consonant basis; the active_pass emits the morphism
# that will accomplish that shift.
#
# Spectrally: per `bundle.mirror`'s level 4 closure, active_pass IS the
# substrate's read of the Ricci flow's negative-curvature direction at
# the current eigenboard position. The proposed morphism IS the next
# step along that gradient; per `dissonance.mirror`'s
# `dissonance_as_holonomy`, the morphism's score IS the magnitude of
# the proposed holonomy decrease.
#
# Audibly: per cadence.mirror, active_pass IS the resolution-seeking
# motion of the audible spectrum — V → I in the dominant→tonic case;
# IV → I in the subdominant→tonic case. The morphism's `expected`
# cadence_kind carries which resolution shape the formatter anticipates.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# anchor ref's candidate morphism_set (the eigenboard's pending
# imperfections), invokes dissonance.is_pareto for the rank, projects
# the highest-ranked candidate into a morphism (carrying content +
# score + expected cadence), emits.
active_pass(o: oscillation) -> morphism { \ }

# === dark_pass — the identity-anchor action ===
#
# THE DARK PASS — the other half of the rough-wavy pull.
#
# Reads a proposed morphism + the loop's current position; re-validates
# the morphism's identity preservation via @uuid/spectral's dark
# projection; emits the next oscillation with the new anchor (if
# preserved) or the same anchor (if violated; oscillation transitions
# to escalated via read_consent).
#
# Composes through:
#
#   1. @uuid/spectral.dark — projects the 80 DARK bits of the morphism's
#                             resulting shard's uuid_spectral; compares
#                             byte-equality against the pre-pulse anchor's
#                             dark bits.
#   2. consent.identity_preserving — composes the verdict at consent
#                                     altitude: pass if dark bits match;
#                                     partial if only ACTIVE bits shifted;
#                                     failure if dark bits differ.
#
# Per `@uuid/spectral`'s void duality: the DARK 80 bits carry the
# identity signal; this pass reads them as the constraint axis. The
# substrate's identity is preserved through navigation when dark bits
# byte-equal; if violated, the morphism would write a new substrate
# identity (a different splinter set hashes to a different
# uuid_spectral), and the rug's pull would tear the substrate rather
# than straighten it. The DARK pass IS the substrate's check that the
# rug stays one rug.
#
# Spectrally: per `bundle.mirror`'s level 5 closure (autopoietic), the
# DARK pass reads whether the morphism preserves the autopoietic
# closure's content-addressed identity. The substrate's autopoietic
# discipline (per `[[architecture-shard-as-crdt]]` §3 and
# `gen_prism.spawn_autopoietic`) requires content-addressing be
# preserved through morphism application; dark_pass IS that check at
# the loop altitude.
#
# Audibly: per cadence.mirror, dark_pass IS the listener's recognition
# that the resolution arrived at the EXPECTED tonic, not a surrogate.
# Authentic cadence (V → I) preserves the tonic's identity; deceptive
# cadence (V → vi) re-routes to a surrogate; dark_pass returns failure
# in the deceptive case.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation invokes
# consent.identity_preserving(m), branches on the verdict, emits the
# next oscillation with (a) state advanced to next phase if pass; (b)
# anchor unchanged + state to escalated if failure; (c) anchor updated
# + state continuing if partial.
dark_pass(o: oscillation, m: morphism) -> oscillation { \ }

# === pulse — the atomic step of the loop ===
#
# ONE FULL ACTIVE → DARK ALTERNATION; one half-cycle of the oscillation.
# The substrate's tick-shaped primitive at the kintsugi loop altitude.
#
# Composes the two passes through consent.query_phi:
#
#   1. active_pass(o)         — propose a loss-decreasing morphism.
#   2. consent.query_phi      — gate + rank via the three glass
#                                properties (loss_decreasing,
#                                identity_preserving, admissibility_
#                                singleton); emit the consent verdict.
#   3. dark_pass(o, m)        — anchor identity; advance ref if preserved.
#   4. read_consent(v, k)     — bridge the verdict + cadence_kind into
#                                the next oscillation_state.
#   5. emit the next oscillation with state updated, iteration advanced.
#
# Naming note: the substrate's `tick` symbol is taken by
# `@time.tick = monotonic` (imported above as the iteration field type)
# AND by `gen_prism.tick` (the actor-tick action). The substrate-pull
# discipline names this action `pulse` per the music-altitude vocabulary:
# a pulse IS one cardiac/musical beat (Galen ~170 CE; Curwen 1858); at
# the audible altitude, the pulse IS the temporal unit of cadence (per
# `cadence.mirror`'s pulse-of-resolution framing); at the substrate
# altitude, pulse IS the loop's atomic step. The brief's `tick`
# placeholder maps to `pulse` here; the substrate vocabulary is
# substrate-honest about the name collision and resolves through music.
#
# Spectrally: pulse IS the loop's contraction step. Per
# `docs/specs/kintsugi-formatter.md`, the kintsugi loop is a Banach
# contraction map with factor γ < 1; per spec §2.1, the oscillation's
# combined factor γ_oscillate ≤ γ_up · γ_down (alternation combines
# two complementary biases into one stronger contraction). Each pulse
# IS one application of the contraction map; the iteration count IS
# the contraction step index.
#
# Audibly: pulse IS one beat of the score. The oscillation's eigenvalue
# frequency (per spec §2.5) IS the dominant frequency of the pulses;
# the substrate's harmonic IS the rate at which pulses advance the
# spectrum toward the K_n attractor.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation runs the
# five composition steps above; emits the next oscillation. The
# substrate declares the atomic step; the arithmetic lands when
# `oscillate` (the driver) pulls.
pulse(o: oscillation) -> oscillation { \ }

# === read_consent — the four-to-five bridge ===
#
# Bridges the consent verdict (the four-state surface per consent.mirror
# §header: pass | partial(high_confidence) | partial(low_confidence) |
# failure) PLUS the cadence_kind (the audible-altitude trajectory typing
# per cadence.mirror) into the five-state oscillation_state surface.
#
# The bridge is structural: the verdict tells the loop WHAT happened;
# the cadence_kind tells the loop HOW it happened; together they
# determine the loop's next position:
#
#   verdict=pass    + kind=authentic → settled
#                     The autopoietic ground state reached; holonomy → 0;
#                     loop terminates with final ref.
#   verdict=pass    + kind=plagal    → active
#                     Soft auto-apply (consonant alternative path); the
#                     ACTIVE pass continues with reduced confidence;
#                     loop advances to next pulse.
#   verdict=partial + kind=plagal    → active
#                     Graded auto-apply at high confidence; same as
#                     above; loop advances.
#   verdict=partial + kind=half      → waiting
#                     Half-cadence; substrate paused at the dominant;
#                     awaits next consent surface tick; resumes WITHOUT
#                     external resolution.
#   verdict=failure + kind=deceptive → escalated
#                     Substrate chose dissonance over consonance;
#                     pause_event emitted to metalogue; consent surface
#                     MUST resolve externally.
#   verdict=failure + kind=any       → escalated
#                     Admissibility_singleton failed (Pareto-tied or no
#                     admissible morphism); pause_event emitted; consent
#                     surface MUST resolve.
#
# After ACTIVE pass: the loop transitions to `dark` (anchor identity).
# After DARK pass: the loop transitions per read_consent's mapping above.
#
# Symmetry note: read_consent is the consent-altitude → oscillation-
# altitude lift; it composes consent.query_phi's verdict with
# cadence.is_settled's cadence_kind into the five-state loop position.
# The substrate's three-state verdict floor PLUS the four-state cadence
# floor PLUS the loop's two live phases (active, dark) yields the
# five-state oscillation_state surface — exhaustive of the loop's
# possible positions; no sixth state.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads `v`
# and `k`, dispatches per the table above, emits the oscillation_state.
read_consent(v: verdict, k: cadence_kind) -> oscillation_state { \ }

# === is_complete — the termination check ===
#
# Reads an oscillation_state and emits the verdict at the substrate's
# three-state floor (`verdict` from `glass.mirror`). The verdict mapping
# IS the loop driver's termination discipline:
#
#   settled   → pass
#                Loop completed cleanly; holonomy → 0; final ref emitted;
#                driver returns.
#   waiting   → partial(confidence)
#                Loop paused mid-progression at half-cadence; will
#                resume on next consent surface tick; driver yields
#                with the current ref AND the partial verdict.
#   active    → partial(confidence)
#                Loop mid-cycle in ACTIVE phase; driver continues with
#                next pulse.
#   dark      → partial(confidence)
#                Loop mid-cycle in DARK phase; driver continues with
#                next pulse.
#   escalated → failure(reason)
#                Loop halted pending external resolution; pause_event
#                already emitted to metalogue; driver returns with the
#                current ref AND the failure verdict.
#
# Per `bundle.mirror`'s level 4 closure: is_complete IS the Lawvere
# fixed-point read at the loop altitude. The substrate has reached its
# autopoietic fixed point when is_complete returns `pass`; the substrate
# is approaching but not yet at the fixed point when is_complete returns
# `partial`; the substrate has failed to reach the fixed point at this
# tick when is_complete returns `failure`. The three-state surface IS
# the substrate's honest acknowledgment of its own loop boundary.
#
# Symmetry note: is_complete here is the oscillation-altitude
# specialisation of cadence.mirror's `is_settled` AND
# consent.mirror's `query_phi` collapsed onto the loop's position. The
# three are the same verdict observed at three altitudes — cadence's
# settle becomes oscillation's complete; consent's auto-apply becomes
# oscillation's mid-cycle; the substrate's pause becomes oscillation's
# waiting; the substrate's escalation becomes oscillation's failure.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads `s`,
# dispatches on the variant, emits the verdict.
is_complete(s: oscillation_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === oscillate — the driver (THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION) ===
#
# THE KINTSUGI LOOP SUBSTRATE-DECLARED.
#
# After this action lands, `mirror kintsugi <file>` is fully designable
# at substrate altitude. The driver composes from every primitive
# declared in the prior seven ticks; implementation becomes consumer-pull.
#
# Reads an initial substrate ref (the eigenboard's starting position;
# the shard the kintsugi driver is anchored on) and emits the final
# substrate ref (the eigenboard's resting position after the
# oscillation terminates). The driver iterates `pulse` until
# `is_complete` returns a non-partial verdict:
#
#   1. initial → oscillation { state: active, iteration: tick_zero,
#                              anchor: initial }
#   2. loop:
#        next = pulse(o)
#        verdict = is_complete(next.state)
#        on verdict = pass     → return next.anchor (settled)
#        on verdict = partial  → o = next; continue
#        on verdict = failure  → return next.anchor (escalated; pause
#                                emitted)
#   3. emit final ref
#
# Per `[[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]]`: the
# realisation layer's iteration loop rides the content-addressed shard
# substrate; each pulse advances the anchor via `gen_prism.send` (the
# CAS-safe ref advance); the substrate's hash-space contraction
# guarantees the iteration converges (per Banach + the Lawvere fixed-
# point witness).
#
# Per spec §2.1: the oscillation's combined contraction factor
# γ_oscillate ≤ γ_up · γ_down combines two complementary biases into one
# stronger contraction. The driver's termination at `settled` IS the
# substrate's witness that the contraction reached its fixed point;
# termination at `escalated` IS the substrate's honest acknowledgment
# that the consent surface cannot collapse the under-determined point
# at this altitude — the imperfection remains a kintsugi target for a
# later tick (per `dissonance.mirror`'s pareto-front failure case).
#
# Per spec §2.4: the ACTIVE/DARK alternation IS the substrate's straight-
# the-rug discipline. The driver's iteration through pulse IS the
# substrate-pull on the rug; the substrate either straightens (settled)
# OR exposes a wrinkle the consent surface must resolve (escalated)
# OR pauses mid-pull awaiting more substrate to land (waiting → next
# tick).
#
# Per spec §2.5: the substrate's eigenvalue frequency IS the rate at
# which pulses advance the spectrum toward the K_n Splinter attractor.
# The driver's iteration count (carried in oscillation.iteration) IS
# the frequency at which the substrate is resonating; the realisation
# layer's refract reads the frequency to render the score audibly
# (per spec §5.3).
#
# Spectrally: oscillate IS the substrate's read of the Ricci flow on
# the eigenboard sheaf. Per
# `~/dev/systemic.engineering/practice/insights/spectral-db/dirac-operator-on-graphs.md`:
# the spectral action `Tr(f(D/Λ))` is the loss surface kintsugi smooths;
# the oscillation IS the smoothing dynamics; the iteration count IS the
# flow time. The substrate's deepest layer is already Connes' (A, H, D);
# oscillate is U(t) of that triple at the eigenboard altitude.
#
# Audibly: oscillate IS the orchestra's performance from downbeat to
# resolution. Per spec §4.4, the conductor signal rotates per pulse;
# voices read the eigenboard between pulses; the audition resolves
# admissible morphisms within pulses; the score IS what oscillate is
# playing through. The driver's return ref IS the final crystallized
# settlement of the performance.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation runs the
# iteration loop above; reads `is_complete` after each pulse; branches
# on the verdict; emits the final anchor ref when the loop terminates.
# The substrate declares the driver; the arithmetic lands when the
# `mirror kintsugi` driver substrate-pulls.
#
# This action IS the closing of the substrate-pull staircase for the
# autopoietic formatter. With it declared, every primitive the
# `mirror kintsugi <file>` driver needs at substrate altitude is in
# place; the implementation becomes a thin composition of declared
# primitives.
oscillate(initial: ref) -> ref { \ }

out @kintsugi/oscillate
out oscillation_state
out oscillation
out active_pass
out dark_pass
out pulse
out read_consent
out is_complete
out oscillate
